<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramagrama</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramagrama was the main town of the Koliyas, a clan republic of the Buddha's time in the foothills of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. Buddhist texts say the Koliyas received a share of the Buddha's relics and built a stupa there, which according to legend was the only original relic stupa that the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a> left unopened. A large brick mound in the Nawalparasi district of Nepal is identified as this stupa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramagrama.jpg" alt="Ramagrama" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sukrat Gaud · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramgram_Stupa_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
